The BMW 3 Series Gran Turismo (F34) Modern Line was a trim level available from the launch of the F30/F34 generation. It was positioned alongside the Sport and Luxury lines, offering a distinct aesthetic focusing on contemporary style with satin aluminum and chrome elements on the exterior and specific interior finishes. It was available with various engine options. The most recent version of the F34 GT was produced until 2020, with a facelift (LCI) in 2016. The Modern Line was available on LCI models as well.

Here's the evaluation based on the characteristics of the F34 GT and the Modern Line trim:

*   **price_usd**: The Modern Line was a premium trim, adding cost over the base model. Prices for a 320i Modern Line in 2013 were around $13,600 - $14,100 used. A new 328i Modern Line Touring (wagon, similar platform) was priced around $73,400 in 2014. A used 318d GT Modern Line was listed for €10,000 (around $10,800 USD). New prices were likely above the market average of $52,000. Score negatively for new price, but used prices are very low. Let's consider the original positioning. Score negatively.
